  "limits": "External Windows/Fedora-GNOME RDP and physical GNOME PRIMARY/AltGr/IME/touchpad acceptance remain BLOCKED: no designated host/account/trust reference or approved physical test seat was available. Loopback authentication, GDK and server-driven reactivation are real integration results, not external-host acceptance. The raw bitmap fixture does not qualify the GNOME/RemoteFX degradation described in [IronRDP #447](https://github.com/Devolutions/IronRDP/issues/447).\n\nKnown product limits: gateway/network fields are metadata, not a routing engine; Remmina conflicts support skip or new identity, without merge-by-ID; group default editing covers display/clipboard while other endpoint overrides remain explicit. Profiles used by an opened tab are conservatively deletion-protected until application restart. SSH terminals use OpenSSH's interactive verification/authentication; Files uses the configured key/agent or Secret Service password, and refuses unknown/changed keys. Encrypted private-key passphrase UI, rsync, recursive transfers and resume are not implemented. Portable SFTP v3 replacement preserves the old file through a backup/restore sequence but is not atomic. A lost connection can leave a named remote partial or backup; connected cancellation cleans its partial. Concurrent changes to a remote namespace are not an atomic SFTP snapshot. Native file chooser upload/download gestures and locked-keyring dialogs still need interactive desktop acceptance; transport integrity uses the production worker through an isolated driver, while panel listing/refresh uses the actual GTK window. File/HTML CLIPRDR, consumer acknowledgement for agent attachments, general termios recovery beyond Bash and daemon/host-crash persistence remain open. RPM/binary publication and product distribution licensing remain unqualified."
